## Status

Self-excluded: **no verified public benchmark numbers** were found for the exact model/ID `kimi-k2.6` in accessible sources at time of research.

## Research notes

- Verified metadata from accessible sources (not benchmark scores): Artificial Analysis lists Kimi K2.6 (Reasoning) as a deprecated open-weights reasoning model (released 2026-04-20) with 1T total / 32B active parameters (MoE), 256k context window, text/image/video input, text output, modified MIT license, and pricing around $0.95/$4.00 per 1M tokens in the fetched snapshot. OpenRouter lists `moonshotai/kimi-k2.6` with broad provider availability and API capabilities.
- Artificial Analysis reported Intelligence Index and task-level benchmark aggregates as unavailable/N/A in the fetched snapshot; no standalone verified benchmark scores (e.g. GPQA, SWE-bench, HLE, MMMU, Terminal-Bench, LiveCodeBench, etc.) for this exact model/ID were found in accessible sources.
- Per `model-report-TEMPLATE.md`: if zero verified public benchmark numbers are found for the exact model/ID, save a notes-only `.md.excluded` file and do not invent placeholder scores.

